          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li#Yablonovitch87
              %p
                Eli Yablonovitch,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Inhibited Spontaneous Emission in Solid-State Physics and Electronics
                %strong 58
                2059 (1987) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.58.2059"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.58.2059
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#John87
              %p
                Sajeev John,
                %em Strong localization of photons in certain disordered dielectric superlattices
                Phys. Rev. Lett.
                %strong 58
                2486 (1987) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.58.2486"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.58.2486
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further articles:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Thomas F. Krauss, Richard M. De La Rue, Stuart Brand,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Two-dimensional photonic-bandgap structures operating at near-infrared wavelengths
                %strong 383
                (1996) 699–702 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/383699a0"}> doi:10.1038/383699a0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#BenistyEtAl99
              %p
                H. Benisty et al.,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Optical and confinement properties of two-dimensional photonic crystals
                %strong 17
                11 (1999) 2063-2077 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1109/50.802996"}> doi:10.1109/50.802996
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                D. N. Chigrin &amp; C. M. Sotomayor Torres,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Periodic thin-film interference filters as one-dimensional photonic crystals
                %strong 91
                (2001) 484–489 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1134/1.1405232"}> doi:10.1134/1.1405232
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Early history:
          %ul
            %li
              David Lindley,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Landmarks – The Birth of Photonic Crystals
              %strong 6
              94 (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://physics.aps.org/articles/v6/94"}> physics:v6/94
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review of experimental realizations:
          %ul
            %li
              Steven G. Johnson,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Photonic Crystals: Periodic Surprises in Electromagnetism
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://ab-initio.mit.edu/photons/tutorial/"} webpage
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://ab-initio.mit.edu/photons/tutorial/L3-fab.pdf"} pdf
          %p and for waveguide arrays:
          %ul
            %li#TrompeterEtAl03
              Henrike Trompeter et al.,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tailoring guided modes in waveguide arrays
              %strong 11
              25 (2003) 3404-3411 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1364/OE.11.003404"}> doi:10.1364/OE.11.003404
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further review:
          %ul
            %li
              Ivan L.Garanovicha, Stefano Longhib, Andrey A.Sukhorukova, Yuri S. Kivshar,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Light propagation and localization in modulated photonic lattices and waveguides
              %strong 518
              1–2 (2012) 1-79 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2012.03.005"}> doi:10.1016/j.physrep.2012.03.005
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On the effective appearance of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schr%C3%B6dinger+equation"} Schrödinger equation
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+waves"} electromagnetic waves
            in photonic crystals:
          %ul
            %li
              Max Lein,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Taking Inspiration from Quantum-Wave Analogies — Recent Results for Photonic Crystals
              %strong 270
              (2018) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.01234"}> arXiv:1804.01234
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-01602-9_10"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-01602-9_10
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              John D. Joannopoulos, Steven G. Johnson, Joshua N. Winn, and Robert D. Meade,
              %em Photonic Crystals: Molding the Flow of Light
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://ab-initio.mit.edu/book/"}> webpage
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/hardcover/9780691124568/photonic-crystals"} ISBN:9780691124568
          %p
            Description of photonic crystals by a
            = succeed ":" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                non-linear Schrödinger equation
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/non-linear+Schr%C3%B6dinger+equation"} ?
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A. Pankov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Periodic Nonlinear Schrödinger Equation with Application to Photonic Crystals
                %strong 73
                (2005) 259–287 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00032-005-0047-8"}> doi:10.1007/s00032-005-0047-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
